# 参考上下文 (Retrieved Context)
以下是从知识库中检索到的类似优秀项目的【设计理念】片段：
---
【案例1 | Science Centre Singapore, Singapore | 来源:world | 区域:未知 | 面积:60,000 sqm (Site Area)】
Designed by architect Raymond Woo, the Science Centre Singapore was conceived as a 'spaceship settled on earth'. The building's main block features a hexagonal design with a 4-storey high central void (The Atrium), creating a monumental impression. The structure rests on truncated pyramidal bases and superimposes hexagonal volumes to house the galleries. The design philosophy focused on accessibility, shifting from a collection-based museum to one centered on self-directed interaction and hands-on discovery. The building was carved out of the National Museum of Singapore to be a separate institution in Jurong East, promoting scientific education in a rapidly industrializing nation.

【案例2 | Universum Bremen, Bremen | 来源:world | 区域:未知 | 面积:Approx. 4,000 sqm (Permanent Exhibition Building) and 2,700 sqm (Special Exhibition Building); Outdoor area 5,000 sqm】
The main Science Center building is an architectural landmark designed by Bremen architect Thomas Klumpp. Resembling a giant silver whale or mussel rising from a water basin, its organic, curved shape is covered by approximately 40,000 stainless steel shingles. In contrast, the adjacent 'SchauBox' (Special Exhibition Building), opened in 2007, is a cubic structure with a rust-red Corten steel façade, designed by Haslob Kruse + Partner. The complex also features a 27-meter high 'Turm der Lüfte' (Tower of the Skies) in the outdoor area.

【案例3 | Science City, Kolkata | 来源:world | 区域:未知 | 面积:68,284 sq. m】
Developed on a 50-acre site that was formerly a municipal garbage dump for over 100 years, representing an ecological reclamation project. The complex features a unique architectural blend of geometric forms: the Dynamotion Hall is designed as a massive spiral ziggurat rising to 38 meters, while the Space Odyssey building features a 23-meter diameter tilted dome. The Convention Centre resembles a tilted saucer with a truncated spherical cone. The extensive landscaping and Science Park integrate the buildings with the environment, dispelling the site's history as a dumping ground.

【案例4 | OMSI (Oregon Museum of Science and Industry), Portland | 来源:world | 区域:未知 | 面积:219,000 sq ft】
Designed by ZGF Architects, the museum occupies a 18.5-acre site on the east bank of the Willamette River. The design concept focuses on the adaptive reuse of the historic Station L power plant, integrating its industrial heritage with modern educational facilities. The exterior features a mix of original industrial brick and concrete structures (the Turbine Hall) and modern additions, characterized by a prominent glass-walled lobby that maximizes natural light and offers dramatic views of the river and downtown Portland. The complex includes a distinctive copper-clad OMNIMAX (now Empirical) theater volume and retains the power plant's massive smokestacks as iconic landmarks.

